# Tests — FY26 Sales Commission Plan: quota relief

Assertion-based tests for `QuotaRelief`. The 30-day gate in S-6.1 is tested
at 29 and at 30 days, each of the three qualifying absence categories is
tested, and the non-qualifying category and the "continuous period" limb are
tested for absence of relief.

Sections then pin the defects the adversarial reviewer found, each of which
produced a plausible number: absence outside the Plan Year (CE-0012), absence
straddling the Plan Year boundary (CE-0013), overlapping absence records
double-counting their shared days (CE-0014), one continuous absence recorded as
two abutting fit-note periods (CE-0028), the S-6.1 reduction rounded to the
penny before Attainment (CE-0027) and an absence covering the whole Plan Year,
which reduces the Quota to nil and used to crash the composition (CE-0026).
Those tests assert a *difference* from the wrong figure as well as the right
one, because the wrong figure is what a careless re-encoding would reproduce —
and the CE-0028 tests assert that the answer is the same whether the absence is
written as one record or two, which is the property the defect broke.

The S-6.2 tests are the important ones. The first composes
`QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota` with `Commission.Attainment` and
`Commission.Accelerator` and asserts that the accelerator computed on the
relieved Quota differs from the one computed on the assigned Quota — which is
the only way to show that the ordering S-6.2 mandates has been honoured rather
than merely described. The last goes through `CommissionAfterRelief`, the scope
in which that ordering is structural rather than remembered, and asserts that
it cannot produce the unrelieved figure.

> Using QuotaRelief
> Using Commission

## Absence fixtures

```catala
declaration absence content QuotaRelief.AbsencePeriod
  depends on
    cat content QuotaRelief.AbsenceCategory,
    d1 content date,
    d2 content date
  equals
    QuotaRelief.AbsencePeriod {
      -- category: cat
      -- start_date: d1
      -- end_date: d2
    }
```

## S-6.1 Day counting — endpoints are inclusive

1 January to 30 January inclusive is 30 days.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS6_1_DayCountInclusive:
  output r content QuotaRelief.QualifyingAbsence

scope TestS6_1_DayCountInclusive:
  definition r equals
    output of QuotaRelief.QualifyingAbsence with {
      -- absence: absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2026-01-01|, |2026-01-30|
    }
  assertion r.days_of_absence = 30
  assertion r.is_qualifying = true
  assertion r.in_year_days_of_absence = 30
```

An absence recorded as starting and ending on the same day is one day.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS6_1_SingleDayAbsence:
  output r content QuotaRelief.QualifyingAbsence

scope TestS6_1_SingleDayAbsence:
  definition r equals
    output of QuotaRelief.QualifyingAbsence with {
      -- absence: absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2026-01-01|, |2026-01-01|
    }
  assertion r.days_of_absence = 1
  assertion r.is_qualifying = false
  assertion r.in_year_days_of_absence = 1
```

## S-6.1 The 30-day gate, on both sides

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS6_1_TwentyNineDaysNoRelief:
  output r content QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota

scope TestS6_1_TwentyNineDaysNoRelief:
  definition r equals
    output of QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota with {
      -- annual_quota: $1,000,000
      -- absence_periods: [
           absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2026-01-01|, |2026-01-29|
         ]
    }
  assertion r.relief_days = 0
  assertion r.relief = $0
  assertion r.relieved_quota = $1,000,000
  assertion r.quota_for_attainment = $1,000,000
```

Thirty days qualifies, and the relief is 30/365ths of the annual Quota:
$1,000,000 x 30/365 = $82,191.78.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS6_1_ThirtyDaysRelieved:
  output r content QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota

scope TestS6_1_ThirtyDaysRelieved:
  definition r equals
    output of QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota with {
      -- annual_quota: $1,000,000
      -- absence_periods: [
           absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2026-01-01|, |2026-01-30|
         ]
    }
  assertion r.relief_days = 30
  assertion r.relief = $82,191.78
  assertion r.relieved_quota = $917,808.22
  assertion r.quota_for_attainment = $917,808.22
```

## S-6.1 Relief is for every day of the absence, not only the days after the thirtieth

A 40-day absence gives 40 days of relief, not 10.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS6_1_ReliefForEveryDay:
  output r content QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota

scope TestS6_1_ReliefForEveryDay:
  definition r equals
    output of QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota with {
      -- annual_quota: $1,000,000
      -- absence_periods: [
           absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2026-01-01|, |2026-02-09|
         ]
    }
  assertion r.relief_days = 40
  assertion r.relief = $109,589.04
  assertion r.relief != $27,397.26
```

