  assertion r.in_year_days_of_absence = 90
```

## S-6.1 "A continuous period" — separate short absences do not combine

Two unconnected 20-day absences total 40 days but neither is a continuous
period of 30 days or more, so neither attracts relief.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS6_1_SeparateAbsencesDoNotCombine:
  output r content QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota

scope TestS6_1_SeparateAbsencesDoNotCombine:
  definition r equals
    output of QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota with {
      -- annual_quota: $1,000,000
      -- absence_periods: [
           absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2026-01-01|, |2026-01-20|;
           absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2026-05-01|, |2026-05-20|
         ]
    }
  assertion r.relief_days = 0
  assertion r.relieved_quota = $1,000,000
```

Two absences that each qualify do accumulate.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS6_1_TwoQualifyingAbsencesAccumulate:
  output r content QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota

scope TestS6_1_TwoQualifyingAbsencesAccumulate:
  definition r equals
    output of QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota with {
      -- annual_quota: $1,000,000
      -- absence_periods: [
           absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2026-01-01|, |2026-01-30|;
           absence of AdoptionLeave, |2026-05-01|, |2026-06-12|
         ]
    }
  assertion r.relief_days = 73
  assertion r.relief = $200,000
  assertion r.relieved_quota = $800,000
```

A qualifying absence alongside a non-qualifying one relieves only the
qualifying days.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS6_1_MixedQualifyingAndNot:
  output r content QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota

scope TestS6_1_MixedQualifyingAndNot:
  definition r equals
    output of QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota with {
      -- annual_quota: $1,000,000
      -- absence_periods: [
           absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2026-01-01|, |2026-03-14|;
           absence of OtherAbsence, |2026-05-01|, |2026-08-31|
         ]
    }
  assertion r.relief_days = 73
  assertion r.relieved_quota = $800,000
```

## S-6.2 Relief is applied before Attainment is calculated

A 73-day long-term sickness absence relieves a $1,000,000 Quota by exactly
$200,000, leaving $800,000. Net Booked Revenue of $800,000 is therefore 100%
Attainment against the relieved Quota, which is band (c) of S-4.1 and an
accelerator of 1.5.

Calculated in the wrong order — Attainment against the assigned $1,000,000
Quota — it would be 80%, which is band (b) and an accelerator of 1.0. The
commission differs by a third. This test asserts the Plan's order and asserts
that the other order gives something else.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS6_2_ReliefBeforeAttainment:
  output relieved content QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota
  output on_relieved_quota content Commission.Attainment
  output on_assigned_quota content Commission.Attainment
  output accelerator_on_relieved content Commission.Accelerator
  output accelerator_on_assigned content Commission.Accelerator

scope TestS6_2_ReliefBeforeAttainment:
  definition relieved equals
    output of QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota with {
      -- annual_quota: $1,000,000
      -- absence_periods: [
           absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2026-01-01|, |2026-03-14|
         ]
    }

  definition on_relieved_quota equals
    output of Commission.Attainment with {
      -- net_booked_revenue: $800,000
      -- quota: relieved.quota_for_attainment_exact
    }

  definition on_assigned_quota equals
    output of Commission.Attainment with {
      -- net_booked_revenue: $800,000
      -- quota: decimal of $1,000,000
    }

  definition accelerator_on_relieved equals
    output of Commission.Accelerator with {
      -- attainment_pct: on_relieved_quota.attainment_pct
      -- new_logo_share: 0%
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
    }

  definition accelerator_on_assigned equals
    output of Commission.Accelerator with {
      -- attainment_pct: on_assigned_quota.attainment_pct
      -- new_logo_share: 0%
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
    }

  assertion relieved.relief_days = 73
  assertion relieved.quota_for_attainment = $800,000
  assertion on_relieved_quota.attainment_pct = 100%
  assertion on_assigned_quota.attainment_pct = 80%
  assertion accelerator_on_relieved.accelerator = 1.5
  assertion accelerator_on_assigned.accelerator = 1.0
  assertion accelerator_on_relieved.accelerator
    != accelerator_on_assigned.accelerator
```

## S-6.1 with no absence at all

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS6_1_NoAbsence:
  output r content QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota

scope TestS6_1_NoAbsence:
  definition r equals
    output of QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota with {
      -- annual_quota: $1,000,000
      -- absence_periods: []
    }
  assertion r.relief_days = 0
  assertion r.relief = $0
  assertion r.quota_for_attainment = $1,000,000
```

## S-6.1 An absence outside the Plan Year relieves nothing — CE-0012

S-1.1 confines the Plan to 1 October 2025 – 30 September 2026 and S-6.1's
1/365th is a proration of that year, so a continuous absence lying wholly in a
different financial year consumes no day of it. The gateway is still passed on
the record's own length — that is the point of keeping the two questions apart —
but there is nothing for it to relieve.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS6_1_AbsenceWhollyAfterPlanYear:
  output gate content QuotaRelief.QualifyingAbsence
  output r content QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota

scope TestS6_1_AbsenceWhollyAfterPlanYear:
  definition gate equals
    output of QuotaRelief.QualifyingAbsence with {
      -- absence: absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2027-01-01|, |2027-06-30|
    }
  definition r equals
    output of QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota with {
      -- annual_quota: $1,000,000
      -- absence_periods: [
           absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2027-01-01|, |2027-06-30|
         ]
    }
  assertion gate.days_of_absence = 181
  assertion gate.is_qualifying = true
  assertion gate.in_year_days_of_absence = 0
  assertion r.relief_days = 0
  assertion r.relief = $0
  assertion r.relieved_quota = $1,000,000
  assertion r.quota_for_attainment = $1,000,000
  assertion r.relief != $495,890.41
```

The mirror image: an absence wholly before the Plan Year. 1 January to 30 June
2024 is 182 days and relieves nothing either.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS6_1_AbsenceWhollyBeforePlanYear:
  output r content QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota

scope TestS6_1_AbsenceWhollyBeforePlanYear:
  definition r equals
    output of QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota with {
      -- annual_quota: $1,000,000
      -- absence_periods: [
           absence of StatutoryParentalLeave, |2024-01-01|, |2024-06-30|
         ]
    }
  assertion r.relief_days = 0
  assertion r.relieved_quota = $1,000,000
  assertion r.relief != $498,630.14
```

## S-6.1 An absence straddling the boundary relieves only its in-year days — CE-0013

Statutory parental leave from 1 August to 30 October 2025 is continuous for 91
days, so the gateway is passed on the whole of it; but only the 30 days from 1
to 30 October 2025 fall in the Plan Year, so the relief is 30/365ths —
$82,191.78 — and not 91/365ths. The 61 days in the preceding financial year
belong to that year's target.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS6_1_AbsenceStraddlingPlanYearStart:
  output gate content QuotaRelief.QualifyingAbsence
  output r content QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota

scope TestS6_1_AbsenceStraddlingPlanYearStart:
  definition gate equals
    output of QuotaRelief.QualifyingAbsence with {
      -- absence: absence of StatutoryParentalLeave, |2025-08-01|, |2025-10-30|
    }
  definition r equals
    output of QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota with {
      -- annual_quota: $1,000,000
      -- absence_periods: [
           absence of StatutoryParentalLeave, |2025-08-01|, |2025-10-30|
         ]
    }
  assertion gate.days_of_absence = 91
  assertion gate.is_qualifying = true
  assertion gate.in_year_days_of_absence = 30
  assertion r.relief_days = 30
  assertion r.relief = $82,191.78
  assertion r.relieved_quota = $917,808.22
  assertion r.quota_for_attainment = $917,808.22
  assertion r.relief != $249,315.07
```

The same at the far end of the year: 1 September to 30 November 2026 is 91
continuous days of which only September's 30 are in the Plan Year.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS6_1_AbsenceStraddlingPlanYearEnd:
  output r content QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota

scope TestS6_1_AbsenceStraddlingPlanYearEnd:
  definition r equals
    output of QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota with {
      -- annual_quota: $1,000,000
      -- absence_periods: [
           absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2026-09-01|, |2026-11-30|
         ]
    }
  assertion r.relief_days = 30
  assertion r.relief = $82,191.78
  assertion r.relieved_quota = $917,808.22
```

## S-6.1 Overlapping records: one day, one 1/365th — CE-0014

Parental leave from 1 October to 30 November 2025 (61 days) and long-term
sickness from 15 October to 15 December 2025 (62 days) overlap over 47 days.
The Employee was absent on every day from 1 October to 15 December 2025 and on
no other — 76 distinct days — so the relief is 76/365ths, $208,219.18. Summing
the records gives 123 days and $336,986.30, which is relief for 47 days on
which the Employee was absent once.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS6_1_OverlappingRecordsCountedOnce:
  output r content QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota

scope TestS6_1_OverlappingRecordsCountedOnce:
  definition r equals
    output of QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota with {
      -- annual_quota: $1,000,000
      -- absence_periods: [
           absence of StatutoryParentalLeave, |2025-10-01|, |2025-11-30|;
           absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2025-10-15|, |2025-12-15|
         ]
    }
  assertion r.relief_days = 76
  assertion r.relief = $208,219.18
  assertion r.relieved_quota = $791,780.82
  assertion r.quota_for_attainment = $791,780.82
  assertion r.relief_days != 123
  assertion r.relief != $336,986.30
```

The same absence recorded twice is one absence.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS6_1_DuplicateRecordCountedOnce:
  output r content QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota

scope TestS6_1_DuplicateRecordCountedOnce:
  definition r equals
    output of QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota with {
      -- annual_quota: $1,000,000
      -- absence_periods: [
           absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2026-01-01|, |2026-03-14|;
           absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2026-01-01|, |2026-03-14|
         ]
    }
  assertion r.relief_days = 73
  assertion r.relief = $200,000
  assertion r.relieved_quota = $800,000
```

An absence longer than the Plan Year relieves the year and no more, so the
relieved Quota reaches nil and never goes below it. 1 October 2025 to 31
October 2026 is 396 continuous days, of which 365 are days of the Plan Year.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS6_1_ReliefCannotExceedTheYear:
  output gate content QuotaRelief.QualifyingAbsence
  output r content QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota

scope TestS6_1_ReliefCannotExceedTheYear:
  definition gate equals
    output of QuotaRelief.QualifyingAbsence with {
      -- absence: absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2025-10-01|, |2026-10-31|
    }
  definition r equals
    output of QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota with {
      -- annual_quota: $1,000,000
      -- absence_periods: [
           absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2025-10-01|, |2026-10-31|
         ]
    }
  assertion gate.days_of_absence = 396
  assertion gate.in_year_days_of_absence = 365
  assertion r.relief_days = 365
  assertion r.relief = $1,000,000
  assertion r.relieved_quota = $0
  assertion r.relieved_quota >= $0
  assertion r.relieved_quota != -$84,931.51
```

## S-6.2 The ordering made structural — CommissionAfterRelief

The reviewer's point about the S-6.2 test above is that it proves the *caller*
can honour the ordering, not that the encoding compels it: `CommissionPayable`
takes `quota` as a free input, and no probe of it can tell a relieved Quota from
an assigned one. `CommissionAfterRelief` takes the assigned Quota and the
absence records instead, and reaches `CommissionPayable` only through
`RelievedQuota`.

On the facts of the note to CE-0012: an assigned Quota of $1,000,000, a 73-day
qualifying absence and Net Booked Revenue of $800,000. Relieved, that is 100%
Attainment, an accelerator of 1.5 and $96,000. Unrelieved it is 80%, an
accelerator of 1.0 and $64,000 — a third less. The test asserts both figures
and that the composing scope produces the first.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS6_2_CommissionAfterReliefIsStructural:
  output composed content QuotaRelief.CommissionAfterRelief
  output unrelieved content Commission.CommissionPayable

scope TestS6_2_CommissionAfterReliefIsStructural:
  definition composed equals
    output of QuotaRelief.CommissionAfterRelief with {
      -- assigned_quota: $1,000,000
      -- absence_periods: [
           absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2026-01-01|, |2026-03-14|
         ]
      -- net_booked_revenue: $800,000
      -- new_logo_share: 0%
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
      -- annual_base_salary: $500,000
    }

  definition unrelieved equals
    output of Commission.CommissionPayable with {
      -- net_booked_revenue: $800,000
      -- new_logo_share: 0%
      -- quota: decimal of $1,000,000
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
      -- annual_base_salary: $500,000
    }

  assertion composed.quota_relief.relief_days = 73
  assertion composed.quota_for_attainment = $800,000
  assertion composed.commission.attainment_calc.attainment_pct = 100%
  assertion composed.commission.accelerator_calc.accelerator = 1.5
  assertion composed.commission_payable = $96,000
  assertion unrelieved.attainment_calc.attainment_pct = 80%
  assertion unrelieved.commission_payable = $64,000
  assertion composed.commission_payable != unrelieved.commission_payable
```

An Employee with no absence is stated as the empty list, and gets the assigned
Quota: the composition is inert where S-6.1 does not bite, which is what makes
it safe to put every commission calculation through it.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS6_2_CommissionAfterReliefWithNoAbsence:
  output composed content QuotaRelief.CommissionAfterRelief

scope TestS6_2_CommissionAfterReliefWithNoAbsence:
  definition composed equals
    output of QuotaRelief.CommissionAfterRelief with {
      -- assigned_quota: $1,000,000
      -- absence_periods: []
      -- net_booked_revenue: $800,000
      -- new_logo_share: 0%
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
      -- annual_base_salary: $500,000
    }
  assertion composed.quota_relief.relief_days = 0
  assertion composed.quota_for_attainment = $1,000,000
  assertion composed.commission.attainment_calc.attainment_pct = 80%
  assertion composed.commission_payable = $64,000
```

## S-6.1 One continuous absence, two abutting records — CE-0028

A 40-day sickness absence certified by two successive fit notes arrives as two
abutting 20-day records with no day of attendance between them. S-6.1's gateway
is "a continuous period of 30 days or more", which is a fact about the absence
and not about the filing, so the two records are one continuous period of 40
days: 40/365ths of a $730,000 Quota is exactly $80,000, leaving $650,000. The
per-record gateway gave this Employee nothing, so the test asserts the nil
answer is *not* produced, and it asserts that the identical absence written as
one record gives the same figure — which is the property the defect broke.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS6_1_AbuttingRecordsAreOneAbsence:
  output split content QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota
  output whole content QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota

scope TestS6_1_AbuttingRecordsAreOneAbsence:
  definition split equals
    output of QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota with {
      -- annual_quota: $730,000
      -- absence_periods: [
           absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2026-01-01|, |2026-01-20|;
           absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2026-01-21|, |2026-02-09|
         ]
    }

  definition whole equals
    output of QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota with {
      -- annual_quota: $730,000
      -- absence_periods: [
           absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2026-01-01|, |2026-02-09|
         ]
    }

  assertion split.relief_days = 40
  assertion split.relief = $80,000
  assertion split.relieved_quota = $650,000
  assertion split.quota_for_attainment = $650,000
  assertion split.relief_days != 0
  assertion split.relief != $0
  assertion split.relief_days = whole.relief_days
  assertion split.quota_for_attainment = whole.quota_for_attainment
```

S-6.1's list of grounds is disjunctive, so a 20-day statutory parental leave
abutting a 20-day long-term sickness absence is also one continuous period of
qualifying absence of 40 days.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS6_1_AbuttingAcrossCategories:
  output r content QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota

scope TestS6_1_AbuttingAcrossCategories:
  definition r equals
    output of QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota with {
      -- annual_quota: $730,000
      -- absence_periods: [
           absence of StatutoryParentalLeave, |2026-01-01|, |2026-01-20|;
           absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2026-01-21|, |2026-02-09|
         ]
    }
  assertion r.relief_days = 40
  assertion r.relief = $80,000
```

A single day of attendance between the two records breaks the continuous
period, and neither 20-day spell reaches 30 days. Merging must not go so far as
to bridge a gap, so this is the other side of CE-0028.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS6_1_OneDayGapBreaksContinuity:
  output r content QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota

scope TestS6_1_OneDayGapBreaksContinuity:
  definition r equals
    output of QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota with {
      -- annual_quota: $730,000
      -- absence_periods: [
           absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2026-01-01|, |2026-01-20|;
           absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2026-01-22|, |2026-02-10|
         ]
    }
  assertion r.relief_days = 0
  assertion r.relieved_quota = $730,000
  assertion r.relief_days != 40
```

A day of some other absence between two sickness records is a day the Employee
was absent on no ground S-6.1 names, so it breaks the period too.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS6_1_NonQualifyingDayBreaksContinuity:
  output r content QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota

scope TestS6_1_NonQualifyingDayBreaksContinuity:
  definition r equals
    output of QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota with {
      -- annual_quota: $730,000
      -- absence_periods: [
           absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2026-01-01|, |2026-01-20|;
           absence of OtherAbsence, |2026-01-21|, |2026-01-21|;
           absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2026-01-22|, |2026-02-10|
         ]
    }
  assertion r.relief_days = 0
```

## S-6.1 The reduction is exact, not rounded to the penny — CE-0027

30 days of statutory parental leave on a $750,000 Quota reduce it by
$61,643.8356164383..., leaving $688,356.1643835616.... S-6.1 specifies no
rounding of that reduction. Against Net Booked Revenue of $344,178.08 the exact
Quota gives Attainment of 49.99999968%, which is S-4.1(a) and an accelerator of
0.0, so no commission is payable. Rounded to the penny the relieved Quota is
$688,356.16 and Attainment is exactly 50.00%, which is S-4.1(b) and an
accelerator of 1.0 — $27,534.25. The test asserts the exact answer, asserts the
rounded denominator would give the other band, and asserts the two differ.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS6_1_ReliefIsNotRoundedToThePenny:
  output composed content QuotaRelief.CommissionAfterRelief
  output on_rounded_quota content Commission.Attainment
  output accelerator_on_rounded content Commission.Accelerator

scope TestS6_1_ReliefIsNotRoundedToThePenny:
  definition composed equals
    output of QuotaRelief.CommissionAfterRelief with {
      -- assigned_quota: $750,000
      -- absence_periods: [
           absence of StatutoryParentalLeave, |2025-11-01|, |2025-11-30|
         ]
      -- net_booked_revenue: $344,178.08
      -- new_logo_share: 0%
      -- commencement_date: |2020-01-01|
      -- annual_base_salary: $120,000
    }

  definition on_rounded_quota equals
    output of Commission.Attainment with {
      -- net_booked_revenue: $344,178.08
      -- quota: decimal of $688,356.16
    }

  definition accelerator_on_rounded equals
    output of Commission.Accelerator with {
      -- attainment_pct: on_rounded_quota.attainment_pct
      -- new_logo_share: 0%
      -- commencement_date: |2020-01-01|
    }

  assertion composed.quota_relief.relief_days = 30
  assertion composed.quota_relief.relief = $61,643.84
  assertion composed.quota_relief.relieved_quota = $688,356.16
  assertion composed.quota_relief.quota_for_attainment_exact > 688356.16
  assertion composed.commission.attainment_calc.attainment_pct < 50%
  assertion composed.commission.attainment_calc.attainment_pct != 50%
  assertion composed.commission.accelerator_calc.accelerator = 0.0
  assertion composed.commission_payable = $0
  assertion on_rounded_quota.attainment_pct = 50%
  assertion accelerator_on_rounded.accelerator = 1.0
  assertion composed.commission.accelerator_calc.accelerator
    != accelerator_on_rounded.accelerator
  assertion composed.commission_payable != $27,534.25
```

## S-6.1 An absence covering the whole Plan Year leaves a nil Quota — CE-0026

Long-term sickness absence from 1 August 2025 to 30 November 2026 covers every
one of the 365 days of the Plan Year, so S-6.1 consumes 365/365ths of the
$1,200,000 Quota and the relieved Quota is nil. That is a lawful outcome and the
Plan answers the question put: S-3.1 multiplies Net Booked Revenue by the Base
Commission Rate and by the accelerator, and Net Booked Revenue is $0, so the
product is $0.00 whatever the accelerator and S-5.1's cap does not bite. The
composition used to raise a division by zero here, on facts S-6.1 compels.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS6_1_NilQuotaIsAnsweredNotRefused:
  output composed content QuotaRelief.CommissionAfterRelief

scope TestS6_1_NilQuotaIsAnsweredNotRefused:
  definition composed equals
    output of QuotaRelief.CommissionAfterRelief with {
      -- assigned_quota: $1,200,000
      -- absence_periods: [
           absence of LongTermSicknessAbsence, |2025-08-01|, |2026-11-30|
         ]
      -- net_booked_revenue: $0
      -- new_logo_share: 0%
      -- commencement_date: |2020-01-01|
      -- annual_base_salary: $120,000
    }
  assertion composed.quota_relief.relief_days = 365
  assertion composed.quota_relief.relief = $1,200,000
  assertion composed.quota_relief.relieved_quota = $0
  assertion composed.quota_for_attainment = $0
  assertion composed.quota_relief.quota_for_attainment_exact = 0.0
  assertion composed.commission.attainment_calc.attainment_pct = 0%
  assertion composed.commission.accelerator_calc.accelerator = 0.0
  assertion composed.commission.cap = $300,000
  assertion composed.commission_payable = $0
```
